# PART 2: GIT WORKFLOW & BRANCH MANAGEMENT

**Reference**: See `MASTER-RULES-INDEX.mdc` for Full Automation Principle and module overview.

## 2.1 Mandatory Pre-Work Steps (NO EXCEPTIONS)

**BEFORE performing ANY action, you MUST execute these commands in this exact order:**

```bash
# 1. Check current branch
git branch --show-current

# 2. Switch to beta if not already on it
git checkout beta

# 3. Pull latest changes
git pull origin beta

# 4. Verify workspace state
git status
```

**DO NOT SKIP THESE STEPS. THEY ARE MANDATORY.**

## 2.2 Feature Branch Creation

**Branch Naming Format**:
```
feature/<issue-description>-<date>-<weekday>-<time>-<am/pm>
```

**Examples**:
- `feature/glfw-include-fix-20251112-Tue-1530-pm`
- `feature/suitesparse-metis-integration-20251113-Wed-0915-am`
- `feature/cuda-mkl-conflict-resolution-20251114-Thu-1400-pm`

**Naming Requirements**:
- Must reflect the issue/feature being handled
- Include date (YYYYMMDD)
- Include weekday (Mon/Tue/Wed/Thu/Fri/Sat/Sun)
- Include time (HHMM, 24-hour format)
- Include am/pm indicator

**Creation Process**:
1. After pulling latest `beta`, create feature branch:
   ```bash
   git checkout -b feature/<issue-description>-<date>-<weekday>-<time>-<am/pm>
   ```
2. Push feature branch immediately:
   ```bash
   git push -u origin feature/<issue-description>-<date>-<weekday>-<time>-<am/pm>
   ```
3. Create PR targeting `beta` with descriptive title:
   - Format: `feat: <issue-description> (<date> <weekday> <time> <am/pm>)`
   - Example: `feat: glfw include fix (2025-11-12 Tue 15:30 PM)`
4. Post PR details in chat immediately:
   - PR URL
   - Source branch
   - Target branch (`beta`)
   - PR title

## 2.3 Git Operations - Explicit User Approval Required

**NEVER run git commands without explicit user approval.**

**Forbidden commands (without approval)**:
- ❌ `git add`
- ❌ `git commit`
- ❌ `git push`
- ❌ `git checkout -b` (branch creation)
- ❌ `git branch <name>`

**Allowed without explicit approval**:
- ✅ `git branch --show-current` - To check current branch
- ✅ `git status` - To check repository status
- ✅ `git checkout <branch>` - To switch to approved branch
- ✅ `git pull origin <branch>` - To sync before starting work

**Required approval phrases from user**:
- For commit: "commit this", "commit changes", "save changes", "add and commit"
- For push: "push to <branch>", "push changes", "push this", "commit and push"
- For branch creation: "create branch", "create feature branch", "start feature branch"

**ONLY after hearing one of these phrases, you may proceed.**

## 2.4 Workflow: Commit → Push → Validation → Merge → Cleanup

**Complete workflow sequence**:

1. **Make changes on feature branch**
   - All work happens on the feature branch
   - Never commit directly to `beta` or `main`

2. **Request commit approval**
   - Show summary of changes
   - List modified files with line ranges and purpose
   - Ask: "Would you like me to commit these changes?"

3. **Upon approval, stage and commit**:
   ```bash
   git add -A
   git commit -m "fix: <description>"
   ```
   - **AUTOMATIC**: If pre-commit hooks fail:
     1. AI agent analyzes hook failures automatically
     2. Auto-fixes ALL fixable issues immediately (batch all fixes)
     3. Stages ALL fixes together: `git add <all-fixed-files>`
     4. Re-runs commit automatically (hooks will pass)
     5. Reports: "Pre-commit hooks failed → Auto-fixed N issues → Re-committed successfully"
     6. **NO USER INTERVENTION**: All handled automatically
     7. **BATCHED**: All fixes applied in single commit (clean build tree)

4. **Request push approval**
   - Ask: "Would you like me to push these changes to the PR branch?"

5. **Upon push approval, push to feature branch**:
   ```bash
   git push origin feature/<issue-description>-<date>-<weekday>-<time>-<am/pm>
   ```

## 2.5 Mandatory Commit & Push Reporting (ALWAYS DISPLAY IN CHAT)

**CRITICAL REQUIREMENT**: After EVERY git push, ALWAYS display in chat:

**Required Information**:
1. **Full commit message** (exactly as committed)
2. **Commit hash** (short or full)
3. **Branch pushed to** (e.g., origin/beta, origin/feature/...)
4. **Push status** (success/failure)
5. **Files changed** (count and list)
6. **GitHub verification link** (if available)

**Display Format** (use this template):
```
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
✅ GIT PUSH COMPLETE - VERIFICATION DETAILS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

COMMIT HASH: <hash>
BRANCH: <branch-name>
REMOTE: origin/<branch-name>

COMMIT MESSAGE:
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ <full commit message - line 1>                    │
│ <full commit message - line 2>                    │
│ ...                                                 │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

FILES CHANGED: <count>
  - <file1>
  - <file2>
  ...

PUSH STATUS: ✅ SUCCESS / ❌ FAILED
VERIFICATION: GitHub link or manual verification instructions

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
```

**WHY THIS IS MANDATORY**:
- Enables cross-verification on GitHub.com later
- Provides audit trail for all commits
- Helps debug if commits don't appear on GitHub
- Essential for team coordination
- Required for compliance tracking

**WHEN TO DISPLAY**:
- ✅ After EVERY `git push` command
- ✅ After automated push (in auto-fix loops)
- ✅ After merge commits
- ✅ After PR merges that push to beta
- ✅ Even if push fails (show error details)

**NEVER SKIP THIS** - This is a mandatory reporting requirement for all git operations.

6. **After push, run validation** (see MASTER-RULES-VALIDATION.mdc - FULL AUTOMATION + BATCHING)
   - **AUTOMATIC**: Validation runs, auto-fixes apply
   - **BATCHED**: All fixes collected → Single commit → Single push
   - **NO USER INTERVENTION**: User only notified of results
   - **CLEAN BUILD TREE**: Minimal pushes (one per validation cycle)

7. **After validation passes, attempt merge** (see MASTER-RULES-MERGE.mdc)

8. **After successful merge, cleanup**:
   ```bash
   git checkout beta
   git branch -d feature/<issue-description>-<date>-<weekday>-<time>-<am/pm>
   git push origin --delete feature/<issue-description>-<date>-<weekday>-<time>-<am/pm>
   ```
   - Close PR (mark as merged)
   - Verify only `main` and `beta` remain
   - **DISPLAY** merge commit details as per section 2.5

